FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: ninety-nine-files.

OFF THE RECORD: a drinking song for clerks. No one drinks, and the
OFF THE RECORD: files do not diminish either, in the long run.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT n IS 99.

ARTICLE 2.
    PROCLAIM THE TRANSCRIPT OF n PLUS " files on the docket, "
        PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF n PLUS " unprocessed files.".
    PROCLAIM "Take one down, stamp it INSUFFICIENT, send it to another office.".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT n IS n LESS 1.
    SHOULD n EXCEED 1, REFER TO ARTICLE 2.

ARTICLE 3.
    PROCLAIM "1 file on the docket, 1 unprocessed file.".
    PROCLAIM "Take it down, stamp it INSUFFICIENT, and the docket is clear.".
    PROCLAIM "The docket is never clear. REFER TO ARTICLE 1.".
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
